          "band": 3,
          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "command-of-evidence-quantitative",
          "passage": "In a 2019 article in Science, Kenneth Rosenberg and colleagues reported a net loss of nearly three billion breeding birds from North America between 1970 and 2017, with grassland species suffering the steepest losses of any biome. Examining their estimates more closely, the researchers distinguished between grassland-obligate species — birds whose breeding range is essentially confined to native grassland — and grassland-associated species, which breed in grasslands but also use other open habitats such as old-field shrublands and roadside edges. The researchers concluded that the obligate species fared considerably worse than the associated species, because _______",
