          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "command-of-evidence-quantitative",
          "passage": "Since the launch of the TOPEX/Poseidon mission in late 1992, NASA's Sea Level Change Portal has tracked global mean sea level (GMSL) using a continuous record of satellite altimeter data. Researchers at NASA's Goddard Space Flight Center who maintain the dataset have argued that the satellite record establishes more than the simple fact that the ocean is rising: it shows that the rate of rise itself has not been constant. A graduate student summarizing the portal's analyses for a public-engagement talk wants to make the case that the satellite altimeter record demonstrates an accelerating rate of global mean sea-level rise across the past three decades, rather than a constant rate of rise sustained throughout the period. The student plans to support that case using the NASA decadal averages reproduced below, because _______",
