          "passage": "In 1902, the archaeologist Zelia Nuttall published *The Codex Nuttall: A Picture Manuscript from Ancient Mexico*, a study of a Mixtec pictorial manuscript that had long sat unstudied in European collections. The codex was no minor ______ its painted pages recorded the genealogies and political alliances of pre-Columbian noble lineages and became a central primary source for the historical study of the Mixtec.",
