          "passage": "Bioarchaeologist Kristina Killgrove, working at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, examines what skeletal remains can reveal about life in Imperial Rome. The strontium isotope ratios in the teeth of individuals buried just outside the city ______ that a substantial fraction of those people had spent their childhoods elsewhere, supporting the long-standing claim that Rome drew migrants from across its empire.",
