          "band": 3,
          "domain": "expression-of-ideas",
          "skill": "transitions",
          "passage": "In her 1957 experiment at Columbia University, the physicist Chien-Shiung Wu cooled a sample of cobalt-60 nuclei to nearly absolute zero and aligned their spins with a strong magnetic field, then counted the electrons emitted in beta decay along the spin direction and against it. She measured a clear asymmetry: significantly more electrons emerged opposite to the spin axis than along it, a pattern that could not arise if the weak interaction respected mirror symmetry. ______ the physics community was forced to abandon the long-standing assumption that parity is conserved in every fundamental interaction.",
