          "passage": "Ophthalmologist Patricia Bath of the UCLA Jules Stein Eye Institute received a U.S. patent in 1988 for an instrument she called the laserphaco probe. The device uses a finely tuned laser pulse to break apart a clouded cataract lens and then aspirates the resulting fragments, a procedure Bath argued ____ the ultrasonic phacoemulsification methods then in standard use among cataract surgeons, because the laser's narrower focus permitted the surgeon to remove the lens with less mechanical disturbance to the surrounding tissue than ultrasonic vibration could deliver.",
