              "text": "Although early readers of *Sex and Temperament in Three Primitive Societies* treated it as a record of inverted gender roles, Mead's central argument was that the wide cross-cultural variation in how temperaments are assigned to men and women indicates that those assignments are largely cultural rather than biological."
