          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "command-of-evidence-quantitative",
          "passage": "A persistent question for archaeologists working on medieval Europe is whether townspeople and rural villagers in the same region ate noticeably different diets, and, if so, in which direction the contrast pointed. One way to attack the question is through bone-collagen chemistry: nitrogen-15 enrichment rises with the share of meat in a person's diet, whereas carbon-13 mostly indexes the cereals and other plant foods at the base of that diet. Comparing skeletal samples drawn from four cemeteries in medieval Hungary — two from villages, two from townsites that were growing during the same centuries — Reitsema and Vercellotti (2012) reported that the dietary contrast between the two settlement types showed up far more strongly in the meat-tracking signal than in the plant-base signal, because ____",
