          "passage": "In *The Boundaries of Blackness* (1999), University of Chicago political scientist Cathy J. Cohen develops the concept of secondary marginalization, the dynamic by which the most stigmatized members of a marginalized group can be pushed to the edges of that group's political life. The slow response of mainstream Black political organizations to the AIDS crisis, on Cohen's account, ______ a clear instance: members of the broader community who were already marginalized along lines of sexuality or drug use were treated as politically inconvenient, even by leaders working to defend the broader community's standing.",
