          "passage": "In *From the War on Poverty to the War on Crime: The Making of Mass Incarceration in America* (2016), Yale historian Elizabeth Hinton argues that federal mass incarceration policies grew directly out of mid-1960s Great Society planning. The expansion of the carceral state, on her account, did not arrive as a sudden punitive ______ it was scaffolded by the same federal administrators who had earlier launched the War on Poverty.",
