          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "form-structure-and-sense",
          "passage": "______ in *Discourse, Consciousness, and Time* (1994), the linguist Wallace Chafe lays out evidence that spoken English unfolds in short intonation units, each corresponding to the limited focus of moment-to-moment consciousness. The book has since become a standard reference for researchers working at the intersection of cognitive science and discourse analysis.",
